    - You can continue using the CLI, but some operations may fail because the API contracts may differ.
    - If an operation fails, first investigate its reported error and more common causes such as command input, local configuration, authentication, network connectivity, or platform state. The CLI itself, especially a development build, may also contain a bug.
    - Only after those causes have been ruled out and API incompatibility still appears likely, try upgrading the CLI to a version compatible with the platform, or contact the platform administrator for support.
